  "notes": "Copper twisted-pair module (Category 5 UTP, max cable length 100 m, BER <10^-12); not an optical transceiver. Document heading says 100BASE-T while body describes 1000BASE-T / 1 Gbps. Features cite 1.25 Gb/s bi-directional; General Specifications data rate 10–1,000 Mb/s. Section 2 title is +3.3V but text states input voltage range +5V +/- 5% and Vcc table 3.13–3.47 V; 3.3 V max not allowed for continuous operation per caution. Power consumption and surge current exceed SFP MSA limits (Is max 375 mA, 1.2 W max; Isurge max 30 mA). LOS indicates received signal below worst-case receiver sensitivity per the standard in use (copper PHY). Ordering table lists related parts QT-SFP-T and QT-SFP-10G-T but this sheet is P/N QT-SFP-M.",
